{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_wave_programme", "label": "v17 gap remediation wave programme", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "Wave order", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight sequential wave PRs (waves share files, so never parallel) plus an ops track with no PRs; all 19 gap issues close before the first production deploy. Order is driven by dependencies: W1 before W6 because both touch attach, W2 before W8, W5 before W7 so the copy pass covers the L description."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w1_money_leaks", "label": "W1 \u2014 money-leaks (wallet merge on attach, undetermined reversal)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wallet merge uses two compensating, bucket-preserving ledger rows inside the attach transaction with advisory locks in sorted order; re-keying the ledger was rejected because it breaks append-only. Undetermined reversals keep the partial-index cap held so no re-mint is possible."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w2_resolver_truth", "label": "W2 \u2014 resolver-truth (entitlement invalidation + status arms)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Broad invalidation on ANY competition write, and a Redis-gated CI suite because ci.yml scopes REDIS_URL to one step today \u2014 this class of defect is structurally invisible until that lands. smoke.ts's manual bustOrgEntitlements workaround is removed so smoke can catch regressions. Invalidation is fail-open by design (300s TTL bounds staleness); competition writes must not fail on Redis errors."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w3_grant_correct", "label": "W3 \u2014 grant-correct (resolved-plan grants, trial qty, month boundary)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Granting on the resolved plan (orgPlanKey) instead of a raw status filter fixes all statuses at once; never hand-copy the SQL CASE. Trial branch grants max(quantity_paid, liveOrgCount) so the billing freeze stays intact. The month boundary bug is a UTC date_trunc issue tested by forcing Europe/London at 23:30 UTC month-end."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w4_credit_economics", "label": "W4 \u2014 credit-economics (instrument, farm-gate, ratify)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Instrument now, weight later \u2014 pack_units per run plus a COGS-vs-sold panel and a 2x-median alert; size-weighted pricing ships only when data shows a real leak. Earn grants are gated on a published-competition-with-division signal so they pay out on real usage. Never-expires is ratified rather than changed, because shipped copy already promises it."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w5_event_pass_l_rung", "label": "W5 \u2014 Event Pass L rung ($59)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Entitlements derived from the M rung so they cannot drift. The purchase picker is an inline radio pair in the upgrade page's ticket stub, NOT a modal: e2e clicks [data-pass-buy] straight through to the Stripe iframe and nothing may be inserted between the click and the money path."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w6_extra_org_addon", "label": "W6 \u2014 extra-org add-on", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exceeding the org cap is a purchase, not an upgrade wall, so both Pro and Pro Plus can buy. Reuses the extra-seat machinery wholesale with the webhook as the single writer of the org_addons row, and must stay idempotent per subscription-item quantity."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w7_truth_in_copy", "label": "W7 \u2014 truth-in-copy with guard tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Quoted numbers are pinned against plan_entitlements and any customer surface naming a retired feature_key fails the suite \u2014 so copy cannot silently drift from the matrix again. Prices link to /pricing, never hardcoded."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w8_pass_ux", "label": "W8 \u2014 pass-UX (eligible / live / ended states)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "W8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Threads the existing isPassLocked predicate rather than copying it; the no-re-buy refusal stays but the sentence tells the truth, leading with data-not-deleted and offering 'Create next year's edition'. A guard test asserts nothing copies competition_passes."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_wave_programme", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w1_money_leaks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "Wave order", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_wave_programme", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w2_resolver_truth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "Wave order", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_wave_programme", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w3_grant_correct", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "Wave order", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_wave_programme", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w4_credit_economics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.md", "source_location": "Wave order", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w6_extra_org_addon", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_26_v17_gap_remediation_design_w1_money_leaks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-v17-gap-remediation-design.